 plant the trees?","correct":"Behind the school.","answers":["Beside a hospital.","At the market.","In the classroom.","Behind the school."],"explanation":"The location is stated directly in the passage.","concept":"comp-2","qa":"v10-reviewed","source":"LatihKu Original","alignment":"KPM-aligned","itemType":"mcq"},{"id":"EN-3-03520","topic":"Grammar","difficulty":"mudah","question":"These ___ my books.","correct":"are","answers":["are","is","be","am"],"explanation":"“These” is plural, so use “are”.","concept":"grammar-3","qa":"v10-reviewed","source":"LatihKu Original","alignment":"KPM-aligned","itemType":"mcq"},{"id":"EN-3-03560","topic":"Tenses","difficulty":"sederhana","question":"Every morning, Siti ___ milk.","correct":"drinks","answers":["drinking","drink","drinks","drank"],"explanation":"A repeated daily action uses the simple present: “drinks”.","concept":"tense-1","qa":"v10-reviewed","source":"LatihKu Original","alignment":"KPM-aligned","itemType":"mcq"},{"id":"EN-3-03460","topic":"Vocabulary","difficulty":"mudah","question":"The opposite of “light” is…","correct":"heavy","answers":["heavy","young","weak","small"],"explanation":"“heavy” is the opposite of “light”.","concept":"ant-light","qa":"v10-reviewed","source":"LatihKu Original","alignment":"KPM-aligned","itemType":"mcq"},{"id":"EN-3-03624","topic":"Prepositions","difficulty":"mudah","question":"The shoes are ___ the bed.","correct":"under","answers":["to","from","under","between"],"explanation":"“under” fits the location or direction in this sentence.","concept":"prep-5","qa":"v10-reviewed","source":"LatihKu Original","alignment":"KPM-aligned","itemType":"mcq"},{"id":"EN-3-03447","topic":"Vocabulary","difficulty":"mudah","question":"The opposite of “near” is…","correct":"far","answers":["happy","far","sad","fast"],"explanation":"“far” is the opposite of “near”.","concept":"ant-near","qa":"v10-reviewed","source":"LatihKu Original","alignment":"KPM-aligned","itemType":"mcq"},{"id":"EN-3-03631","topic":"Sentence","difficulty":"mudah","question":"Choose the correct sentence.","correct":"She likes reading books.","answers":["She books likes reading.","She likes reading books.","Likes she reading books.","She like reading books."],"explanation":"The subject and verb agree, and the word order is correct.","concept":"sentence-0","qa":"v10-reviewed","source":"LatihKu Original","alignment":"KPM-aligned","itemType":"mcq"},{"id":"EN-3-03498","topic":"Grammar","difficulty":"mudah","question":"She ___ to school every day.","correct":"goes","answers":["gone","going","goes","go"],"explanation":"With “she” in the simple present, use “goes”.","concept":"grammar-0","qa":"v10-reviewed","source":"LatihKu Original","alignment":"KPM-aligned","itemType":"mcq"},{"id":"EN-3-03617","topic":"Prepositions","difficulty":"mudah","question":"The picture is ___ the wall.","correct":"on","answers":["to","from","under","on"],"explanation":"“on” fits the location or direction in this sentence.","concept":"prep-4","qa":"v10-reviewed","source":"LatihKu Original","alignment":"KPM-aligned","itemType":"mcq"},{"id":"EN-3-03598","topic":"Prepositions","difficulty":"mudah","question":"The cat is ___ the box.","correct":"in","answers":["with","from","in","to"],"explanation":"“in” fits the location or direction in this sentence.","concept":"prep-1","qa":"v10-reviewed","source":"LatihKu Original","alignment":"KPM-aligned","itemType":"mcq"},{"id":"EN-3-03589","topic":"Prepositions","difficulty":"mudah","question":"The book is ___ the table.","correct":"on","answers":["between","at","on","from"],"explanation":"“on” fits the location or direction in this sentence.","concept":"prep-0","qa":"v10-reviewed","source":"LatihKu Original","alignment":"KPM-aligned","itemType":"mcq"},{"id":"EN-3-03581","topic":"Tenses","difficulty":"sederhana","question":"Now, the children are ___ in the park.","correct":"playing","answers":["play","plays","playing","played"],"explanation":"After “are”, use the -ing form for an action hap